/// Bandit.HTTP2.StreamProcess: one process per stream, running the
/// pipeline. Spawned monitored by the connection when a stream's first
/// HEADERS arrives, and stops normally when done. The connection learns
/// of the end through the DOWN message and resets or forgets the stream
/// there — the stream process never waits on its own mailbox.
///
/// An Actor started with `spawnMonitoredAsyncWith:` (BT-4781), which
/// answers `{actor, ref}` at once without waiting for the new process's
/// `initialize` (BT-4477; before it, `Actor spawn` made the connection
/// wait for each stream's init in its own loop, BT-4469, and this was a
/// plain `spawn_monitor` process). Nothing calls a stream process: the
/// pipeline runs in a `continueWith:` step requested by `initialize`, which
/// then stops the actor, so no message is sent to it. The connection must
/// call `spawnMonitoredAsyncWith:` itself, from its own methods: the
/// monitor belongs to the process that runs the spawn, and a class method
/// here would run in the class's process. The actor process carries the
/// `$beamtalk_actor` => `StreamProcess` marker that tools (the stress
/// tests' stream killer) use to find stream processes.
///
/// An abnormal end (a leaked raise past the pipeline's own handling)
/// is swallowed here the way Bandit's handle_error returns normally:
/// the 500 already went out through sendOnError, and the connection
/// resets the stream on the DOWN message.
typed Actor subclass: StreamProcess
  state: transport :: HTTP2Stream
  state: handler :: ExchangeHandlerLike
  state: config :: BuccaneerConfig
  state: connData :: Tuple(Boolean, Tuple | Symbol)
  state: span :: CatalinaTelemetry | Nil = nil

  initialize -> Nil =>
    self continueWith: #run
    nil

  /// The stream process body: run the pipeline, then stop.
  run -> Nil =>
    [
      Pipeline
        runRequest: self.transport
        handler: self.handler
        connectionSpan: self.span
        connData: self.connData
        options: self.config
    ] on: Exception do: [:e :: Exception | nil]
    self stopWith: #normal
    nil
